       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day (850 mg three times daily), with a maximum of 1,000 mg per dose in most references.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about 5 times that maximum. It carries a serious risk of toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **425 mg** by mouth three times daily (this isn't a standard tablet strength, so the dose may need adjusting)\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily, or another dose\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 4250 mg really is what you want, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending first."
